.TH NFTBAN-SURICATA 8 "2025-12-28" "NFTBan 1.0.14" "NFTBan Manual"
.SH NAME
nftban\-suricata \- Suricata IDS/IPS integration for NFTBan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nftban suricata
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nftban suricata
provides automated installation, configuration, and management of Suricata IDS (Intrusion Detection System) integration with NFTBan firewall.

Suricata analyzes network traffic for threats using signature-based detection rules and generates alerts in EVE JSON format. NFTBan processes these alerts and automatically blocks malicious IPs using nftables.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Automatically install Suricata IDS with NFTBan-optimized configuration.
Checks for package availability (EPEL/APT), downloads ET/Open ruleset, and configures systemd services.

.TP
.B enable
Enable and start Suricata service. Also enables weekly automatic rule updates timer.

.TP
.B disable
Stop and disable Suricata service and automatic updates.

.TP
.B status
Display comprehensive status including:
.RS
- Installation and version information
.RE
.RS
- Service running/enabled status
.RE
.RS
- Automatic update timer status
.RE
.RS
- Rule count and recent alerts
.RE

.TP
.B rules update
Manually download latest detection rules from ET/Open source and restart Suricata.

.TP
.B rules list
List all installed rule files in /var/lib/suricata/rules/

.TP
.B help
Display detailed help message with examples.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Complete automated installation:
.B sudo nftban suricata install && sudo nftban suricata enable

.TP
Check status:
.B nftban suricata status

.TP
View live alerts:
.B tail -f /var/log/nftban/suricata/eve-alerts.json | jq 'select(.event_type=="alert")'

.TP
Manual rule update:
.B sudo nftban suricata rules update

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml
Main Suricata configuration file (NFTBan-optimized)

.TP
.I /var/lib/suricata/rules/
Installed detection rules (ET/Open ruleset)

.TP
.I /var/log/nftban/suricata/eve-alerts.json
Alert output in EVE JSON format

.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/nftban-suricata-update.timer
Systemd timer for weekly rule updates (Sunday 3 AM)

.TP
.I /etc/nftban/nftban.conf
NFTBan configuration with IDS integration flags

.SH INTEGRATION
.SS DDoS Module
Enable IDS-assisted DDoS detection:
.PP
.RS
.B nftban ddos enable
.br
.B echo "DDOS_MODE=suricata" >> /etc/nftban/conf.d/ddos/main.conf.local
.RE

.SS Portscan Module
Enable IDS-assisted portscan detection:
.PP
.RS
.B nftban portscan enable
.br
.B echo "PORTSCAN_MODE=suricata" >> /etc/nftban/conf.d/portscan/main.conf.local
.RE

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B System
2+ CPU cores, 2+ GB RAM, 1+ GB free disk

.TP
.B Software
NFTBan v1.0.14+, Python 3, pip3, EPEL repository (RHEL/Rocky)

.TP
.B Network
Internet access for rule downloads

.SH PERFORMANCE
.TP
.B CPU Usage
10-30% of 1 core (typical VPS traffic)

.TP
.B Memory Usage
300-800 MB resident

.TP
.B Latency
Alert to block: 300-500ms typical

.SH AUTOMATIC UPDATES
Rules are automatically updated weekly via systemd timer:
.TP
.B Schedule
Sunday 3:00 AM ± 1 hour randomization

.TP
.B Persistence
Missed updates run after reboot

.TP
.B Manual Trigger
.B systemctl start nftban-suricata-update.service

.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B Service won't start
.RS
Check if rules are installed:
.B nftban suricata rules update
.RE

.TP
.B No alerts generated
.RS
Test with: curl http://testmyids.com
.RE

.TP
.B High CPU usage
.RS
Reduce workers in /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml to match CPU cores
.RE

